# The format of this file is identical to `.dockerignore`.
# It is used to reduce the size of deployed images to make the process of publishing faster.

# No need to store the pnpm store twice.
.local

# Git history is not needed in the production image (~2.4 GB savings).
.git

# Dev-only backup files.
.migration-backup

# Build-time source assets — already bundled into dist by the build step.
attached_assets

# Legacy media (~3.4 GB). These are NOT served in production and never have
# been: under the previous Autoscale target they were excluded from the build
# entirely, which is exactly why restoreRecipeImagesFromUploadsOnce() exists to
# copy them into Object Storage. The deploymentTarget is now "gce", which ships
# the whole filesystem, so they were being pushed on every publish for nothing
# and took the Repl layer over the size it can push.
#
# The express.static mounts on /uploads and /videos keep working: they resolve
# to nothing in production (as before), and every multer write destination
# does mkdirSync(recursive) so uploads still work.
#
# ROOT-LEVEL ONLY. This must not match dist/public — that is the built
# frontend and excluding it would serve a blank site.
/uploads
/public

# Build cache, regenerated on every install.
.cache

# Defensive: whatever matches above, the build output must always ship.
# dist/public IS the site. Later patterns win in .dockerignore, so these
# exceptions guarantee it survives.
!dist
!dist/**
